<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peshwa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Peshwas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peshwa was the chief minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state, an office that became hereditary and the effective seat of power in the eighteenth century. Peshwas such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balaji-vishwanath">Balaji Vishwanath</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baji-rao-i">Baji Rao I</a> expanded Maratha territory northwards. Under them the Maratha Empire became a confederacy of semi-autonomous chiefs, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrapati">Chhatrapati</a> retained ceremonial supremacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peshwa.jpg" alt="Peshwa" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Internet Archive Book Images · No restrictions · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bajirao_II_Peshwa_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
